  <Properties>
    <mainContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "7e5b24ac-fc8e-4b56-93b7-9820810ef7d7",
      "key": "f61b49a6-efa2-40d2-a828-1e84d683e1aa",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch2\u003EDear decaf\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou sit on the bottom shelf, in a bag with a green sticker, waiting for someone to choose you after nine at night. Perry has been that someone for years, and it is time somebody said it out loud: decaf, you deserve better than the jokes.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe jokes are well worn. Why bother? What is the point? The point is a warm cup in the evening that does not keep you up until the early hours counting ceiling tiles. The point is flavour without the shakes. The point is that people who love coffee also love sleep, and for once the two can coexist.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EA fair hearing\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EModern decaf is a different animal from the tired, papery stuff of old. Good beans are gently decaffeinated using water or sparkling methods that leave much of the flavour behind. Buy it fresh, grind it just before brewing, and treat it with the same respect as any other bean.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIt will not wake you up, and it never promised to. It simply sits next to you on the sofa and gives you the taste, the ritual and the warm mug, asking for nothing in return. Perry thinks that is a rather lovely thing to be, and has decided to raise a cup to it tonight.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "settingsData": [],
